# Architecture Overview: Hybrid LLM Design

- Not multiple separate LLMs: one fine-tuned model given task-specific input structures
- BERT classifier routes emails into 4 active categories (summarize removed from classifier)
  - Reply, Compose, Plan/Schedule, Other
  - Summarize handled via dedicated button, not classification
- Each category triggers a specialized skill/prompt on Amazon Bedrock

# Planning and Scheduling Workflow

- Agreed approach: LLM extracts structured JSON from email body (date, time, attendees, duration, timezone)
  - Backend parses JSON deterministically, no agentic loop needed
  - Backend calls Google Calendar API to check availability
- Proposed time constraints: 9 AM to 5 PM only (baked into planning skill/prompt)
- Slot selection UI: ChatGPT-style multiple choice with a free-text override field
  - User picks a slot, backend books it and LLM drafts the reply
  - If user disputes a slot, cycle repeats until confirmed
- Two LLM calls for scheduling: planning LLM extracts intent, main LLM drafts the reply

# Amazon Bedrock Flow Builder

- Flow Builder identified as a strong fit for orchestrating the scheduling workflow
- Proposed flow: email in → intent router → validate/resolve dates → check calendar → compose reply → user review → send/create event → store outcome
- Configured Prompt Routers can route between planning LLM and main LLM
- BERT classifier can potentially trigger Bedrock flows directly
- Separate flows for each of the 5 task categories under consideration

