# Summarize Feature

- Triggered by a dedicated button (not typed prompt, not classifier)
- Clicking an email shows a “Summarize this thread” button → summary appears in chatbox
- Follow-up questions on the email (e.g. “what’s in thread 3?”) fall under “Other” category
  - Each follow-up passes full email thread + user question to LLM (no prior LLM responses)
  - Rationale: passing prior LLM responses adds latency and repetition

# Reply and Compose Features

- Reply button added alongside Summarize for one-click draft generation
  - User can still type “reply to this email saying X” for custom prompts
  - Button reduces classifier load (though BERT classification is ~0.01ms, largely negligible)
- Backend passes sender info (from/to fields) to LLM for all tasks
  - Handles edge case where email signature is an image (not parseable text)
  - Username stored in backend; passed as JSON variable to LLM
- Compose also receives from/to for accurate sign-off generation

